	<unit id="PilotLog.Stats.CompletionRange" >				
		<notes>
			<note>
				The {collection} variable contains the name of the mission collection, such as "Y-wing Historical Missions"
				The {range} variable will look like "1, 3, 5-10" and indicates which missions in the collection have been completed.
				If no mission has been completed, then the {range} variable will contain the text in the PilotLog.Stats.NoCompletion string below.
			</note>
		</notes>
        <segment>
          <source>{collection} (Completed {range})</source>
          <target>{collection} (Completadas {range})</target>
        </segment>
	</unit>
	<unit id="PilotLog.Stats.NoCompletion" >				
		<notes>
			<note>
				This makes reference to no mission in a collection having being completed. 
				It will appear as the {range} variable in the PilotLog.Stats.CompletionRange string above.
			</note>
		</notes>
        <segment>
          <source>none</source>
          <target>ninguna</target>
        </segment>
	</unit>
